    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**Prioritise it for the next study, provisionally.** The nominal margin is:\n\n`30 \u00b5M / 0.05 \u00b5M = 600-fold`\n\nThat is reassuring for hERG at the intended free exposure, but it is not by itself a cardiac-safety conclusion. The comparison is only valid if the IC50 is appropriately corrected for free drug in the assay and the Cmax is a reliable unbound peak exposure.\n\n**Test next:**\n\n1. **Confirm hERG concentration-response** using a fit-for-purpose patch-clamp assay, including assay free-drug correction and IC10/IC20 as well as IC50.\n2. **Measure exposure margins at supra-therapeutic doses**, including free Cmax and relevant active metabolites.\n3. If confirmation remains clean, run **in vivo cardiovascular telemetry** at intended and adequately higher exposures, with QT/QTc, heart rate, blood pressure, and arrhythmia monitoring.\n4. Add Nav1.5/Cav1.2 testing if the compound has structural or pharmacological reasons to raise broader ion-channel concern.\n\nA result that would change prioritisation is substantial hERG inhibition at clinically relevant free concentrations, an active metabolite with a much smaller margin, or QT effects in telemetry despite the in-vitro margin.",
